  "assessment": [
    "All final-source measurements and checks passed. At horizon 128 the machine correction median across current runs was 36.070-40.378 microseconds for 8-byte application state and 393.320-407.138 microseconds for 64 KiB. These are fixture observations, not latency guarantees.",
    "Both paths perform the same application arithmetic and correction. The machine path additionally carries machine head/context/provenance and owned state transitions; its state storage and snapshot digest are larger. Do not treat the difference as a safety-equivalent legacy regression or attribute it to one component.",
    "The native comparator uses the pre-existing API on the current engine, not a v0.4 binary. Frozen old-fixture comparisons remain separate and their outstanding review flags are unchanged.",
    "This fills the bounded timeline-over-machine measurement profile. Native end-to-end execution, broader payload/effect profiles, full chaos and exact release qualification remain open."
  ],
